2026-10-25T03:15:38.2945270Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3004270Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3005790Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3006860Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3007210Z 
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3008080Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3008750Z 
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3009040Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3009440Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3009690Z 
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3012360Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3012860Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3013970Z 
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3014320Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T03:15:38.3014700Z   $ sh ./install-nix
